<article class="env-lemma" id="08IJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08IJ">Lemma <span data-tag="08IJ">75.6.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be an affine morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. For $E$ in $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$ we have $Rf_* Lf^* E = E \otimes ^\mathbf {L}_{\mathcal{O}_ Y} f_*\mathcal{O}_ X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $f$ is affine the map $f_*\mathcal{O}_ X \to Rf_*\mathcal{O}_ X$ is an isomorphism (Cohomology of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/073H" data-tag="073H">69.8.2</a>). There is a canonical map $E \otimes ^\mathbf {L} f_*\mathcal{O}_ X = E \otimes ^\mathbf {L} Rf_*\mathcal{O}_ X \to Rf_* Lf^* E$ adjoint to the map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  Lf^*(E \otimes ^\mathbf {L} Rf_*\mathcal{O}_ X) = Lf^*E \otimes ^\mathbf {L} Lf^*Rf_*\mathcal{O}_ X \longrightarrow Lf^* E \otimes ^\mathbf {L} \mathcal{O}_ X = Lf^* E  \]
</div>
    <p>
       coming from $1 : Lf^*E \to Lf^*E$ and the canonical map $Lf^*Rf_*\mathcal{O}_ X \to \mathcal{O}_ X$. To check the map so constructed is an isomorphism we may work locally on $Y$. Hence we may assume $Y$ and therefore $X$ is affine. In this case the problem reduces to the case of schemes (Derived Categories of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/08I9" data-tag="08I9">36.5.3</a>) via Lemma <a href="/tag/071Q" data-tag="071Q">75.4.2</a> and Remark <a href="/tag/08GH" data-tag="08GH">75.6.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>